{
  "case_id": "2018-17-1702",
  "document_hash": "a870611aae1bda5ee688b19c191430b90cee6d6b8b491398aa82939446ef9252",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1702",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a870611aae1bda5ee688b19c191430b90cee6d6b8b491398aa82939446ef9252",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a870611aae1b-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I'm sorry. It just means it's a mixed actor, meaning you can -- it has its own speech. Government often has its own speech. So that it can create speech, I don't think, means anything. Similarly, time, place regulations, that anybody can do that or -- or whether it's the government or a private actor with respect to property."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1702",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a870611aae1bda5ee688b19c191430b90cee6d6b8b491398aa82939446ef9252",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a870611aae1b-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you have the power to say this evening we wish to discuss subways; tomorrow at 4:00, we will discuss the public schools? All right. Do you have that power?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. De Leeuw",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1702",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a870611aae1bda5ee688b19c191430b90cee6d6b8b491398aa82939446ef9252",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a870611aae1b-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We -- we still win under Jackson. We think that the -- that the lack of discretion does not convert us into a state actor. Under Jackson, under Sullivan, under all the cases that have looked at pervasive regulation, that has never been held to be enough to convert a private party's action into that of the state. In Rendell-Baker, Blum, the entire series of cases that have looked at that issue, they've all held that regulation, even pervasive regulation, is not sufficient."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Hughes",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1702",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a870611aae1bda5ee688b19c191430b90cee6d6b8b491398aa82939446ef9252",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a870611aae1b-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This is a public forum because New York has generally opened property that it controls for speech. New York has a general access policy. That's -- this is its first-come, first-served policy. And I think the critical feature here, which Petitioners cannot dispute, is that MNN lacks discretion not to -- that they cannot decline to run content that is protected by the First Amendment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1702",
      "confidence": 0.92,
      "document_hash": "a870611aae1bda5ee688b19c191430b90cee6d6b8b491398aa82939446ef9252",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a870611aae1b-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The critical thing is, if the hot dog program wants to come on, there's nothing MNN can do to say you cannot access this forum. It's the same way of going to Central Park. If you're, you know, the hot dog speaker and you want to go to Central Park and speak that message, you have the right to do so because it's a policy of general access."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1702",
      "confidence": 0.88,
      "document_hash": "a870611aae1bda5ee688b19c191430b90cee6d6b8b491398aa82939446ef9252",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a870611aae1b-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the states and localities have complete control as to decide whether they want to have a system that New York has that leads to these First Amendment consequences or if they prefer to have a system, for example, as California has."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1702",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "a870611aae1bda5ee688b19c191430b90cee6d6b8b491398aa82939446ef9252",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a870611aae1b-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Could you have just sued the city and not MNN?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1702",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a870611aae1bda5ee688b19c191430b90cee6d6b8b491398aa82939446ef9252",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a870611aae1b-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, if the government imposes a first-come, first-served requirement on a private company --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1702",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a870611aae1bda5ee688b19c191430b90cee6d6b8b491398aa82939446ef9252",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a870611aae1b-0003-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But it's not so clearly different because, in the United States, there are vast numbers of different kinds of arrangements between government and private people, ranging from agency to General Motors."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1702",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a870611aae1bda5ee688b19c191430b90cee6d6b8b491398aa82939446ef9252",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a870611aae1b-0003-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 76,
        "start": 76
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
